  "quantiser": "nearest, ties toward zero. Pinned by the RED channel: w=0 reads 127 from an exact 127.5 (so ties go down) and w=0.05 reads 134 from 133.875 (so it is nearest and not truncation). This describes the REFERENCE's float->byte conversion, not ours -- ours is the GL pipeline's. It lives in the test, never in source/.",
  "near_tie_divergence": "At products within ~0.05 LSB ABOVE a rounding tie the reference rounds DOWN where nearest-rounding goes up. Two instances are present in these cells and no more: green at w=0.4257143 (81 vs 80) and blue at w=0.2114286 (101 vs 100). Attributed to the CONVERSION and not to any constant, because blue's neutral (0.5) was never in dispute and is exact on thirteen cells, yet fails at its own thinnest margin exactly as green does at its. The test asserts this list; it does not widen a tolerance.",
